{"id": "sfusd-pay-reported-outside-regular-wages", "title": "Why did San Francisco schools report so much compensation as “other pay”?", "seconds": 63.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.08, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "6ccc1faf78c808f3", "words": 176, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[0]"], "text": "San Francisco Unified reported 131,424,325 dollars in other pay for 2021.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 6.92, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["What", "counted", "as", "other", "pay?"], "sub": "San Francisco Unified"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.9, 1.43, 1.86, 2.16, 2.37, 2.73, 3.32, 3.63, 3.94, 4.31, 4.75, 4.94, 5.2, 5.47, 5.64, 6.01]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[0]"], "text": "That came to 26.84 dollars for every 100 dollars of regular pay.", "t0": 7.04, "t1": 11.83, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "y2021", "kicker": "California State Controller’s Office", "text": "State payroll report", "mark": "State payroll report"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.47, 0.57, 1.16, 1.55, 1.68, 2.22, 2.55, 2.73, 2.99, 3.22, 3.52, 3.89, 3.99, 4.41]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The difference is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 11.95, "t1": 13.91, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A reporting comparison"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.5, 0.64, 0.73, 1.13, 1.31, 1.39]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "The middle result among ten other large reporting employers was 7.30 dollars.", "t0": 14.03, "t1": 18.78, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Per $100 of regular pay", "heading": "2021 comparison", "source": "y2021", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "San Francisco Unified", "value": "$26.84"}, {"icon": "audit", "label": "Median of ten other large employers", "value": "$7.30"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 0.83, 1.14, 1.41, 1.66, 1.99, 2.41, 2.94, 3.11, 3.43, 3.82, 3.92, 4.26]}, {"scene": "years", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "The district ranked first in all six years it appeared.", "t0": 19.0, "t1": 21.84, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "exports", "kicker": "California State Controller’s Office", "text": "State K–12 pay files", "mark": "State K–12 pay files"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.57, 0.87, 1.23, 1.41, 1.63, 1.9, 2.21, 2.3]}, {"scene": "years", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]", "established[5]"], "text": "The comparison includes reporting employers with at least 5,000 paid positions.", "t0": 21.96, "t1": 26.35, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "5,000 paid positions"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.71, 1.11, 1.58, 2.08, 2.25, 2.34, 2.59, 2.93, 3.33, 3.64]}, {"scene": "years", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "Schools report voluntarily. The district is absent in 2020 and from 2022 through 2024.", "t0": 26.47, "t1": 33.32, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "rules", "kicker": "California State Controller’s Office", "text": "Voluntary reporting", "mark": "Voluntary reporting"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.55, 0.94, 2.24, 2.42, 2.84, 3.02, 3.47, 3.6, 3.93, 4.38, 4.55, 4.75, 5.06, 5.64, 5.85, 6.14]}, {"scene": "years", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "The state reports lump sums and overtime in separate columns.", "t0": 33.44, "t1": 36.79, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "y2021", "kicker": "California State Controller’s Office", "text": "Separate payroll columns", "mark": "Separate payroll columns"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.42, 0.86, 1.14, 1.58, 1.77, 2.29, 2.39, 2.7]}, {"scene": "district", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "The district’s fiscal 2021 parcel-tax audit lists retention bonuses and paraprofessional stipends.", "t0": 37.01, "t1": 43.39, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "qtea", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District, independent audit by Eide Bailly LLP", "text": "Parcel-tax fund", "mark": "Parcel-tax fund"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.6, 1.09, 1.42, 2.03, 2.86, 3.23, 3.47, 3.99, 4.6, 4.76, 5.61]}, {"scene": "district", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "The separate compliance audit tested 11,987,250 dollars of district payroll.", "t0": 43.51, "t1": 47.82, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "compliance", "kicker": "San Francisco Unified School District, independent audit by Eide Bailly LLP", "text": "Permissible uses", "mark": "Permissible uses"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.49, 1.12, 1.45, 1.81, 2.06, 2.45, 2.82, 3.22, 3.32, 3.73]}, {"scene": "district", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "It reported no exception when testing spending against the parcel-tax measure.", "t0": 47.94, "t1": 51.87, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "No exception in this procedure"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.56, 0.72, 1.23, 1.41, 1.85, 2.27, 2.63, 2.73, 3.45]}, {"scene": "district", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[3]", "established[4]"], "text": "The audit covers a fiscal year. The statewide payroll file covers a calendar year.", "t0": 51.99, "t1": 56.5, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Different reporting periods"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.48, 0.84, 0.91, 1.34, 1.84, 2.01, 2.53, 2.94, 3.27, 3.6, 3.67, 4.17]}, {"scene": "district", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "next[0]"], "text": "The district’s payroll codes would show what made up the reported total.", "t0": 56.62, "t1": 60.09, "shot": "r12", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["District payroll codes", "Other employers’ payroll codes"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.59, 1.05, 1.41, 1.6, 1.83, 2.01, 2.25, 2.41, 2.52, 3.01]}, {"scene": "district", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 60.21, "t1": 62.35, "shot": "r13", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.42, 0.53, 0.59, 1.07, 1.26, 1.35]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Other pay", "years": "Six reported years", "district": "What was paid?"}, "look": "flow", "hook": "number"}